<BaseLayout title="About | Yetyellow" description="Engineering leadership and a practical focus on AI adoption.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Engineering leadership, with a practical focus on AI adoption.</h1>
  </section>
  <section class="two-column-copy">
    <aside><p class="section-label">Identity</p><p class="identity-name">Ljupcho<br />Stojcheski</p></aside>
    <div>
      <p class="large-copy">I lead cross-functional engineering work and have spent 20 years working across software delivery, systems and organisational change.</p>
      <p>Yetyellow is where I build practical experience with AI, automation and agentic systems. I use it to test ideas, learn from the work and form a clearer view of what teams and leaders need to make AI useful.</p>
      <p>I am interested in the gap between a promising demonstration and a working team practice. That gap involves workflow design, team capability, controls and leadership choices. It is where most of the work sits.</p>
      <p>This site supports conversations with engineering leaders who are working through the same questions. I will publish work here when it is useful to share, including where it fell short.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
